    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 147,
        "endIndex": 453,
        "text": "#### **Candidate [1] | WSJ: Effective Altruism's influence on Anthropic & early employee land purchases**\n* **What is confirmed:** *The Wall Street Journal* published an in-depth report detailing how Effective Altruism (EA) philosophy and catastrophic AI risk concerns shaped Anthropic’s founding culture"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 455,
        "endIndex": 634,
        "text": "The report confirmed that several early Anthropic employees previously discussed or considered buying remote land in the US to relocate to in the event of an existential AI crisis"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 636,
        "endIndex": 831,
        "text": "* **Important caveats:** The relocation plans reflect personal/cultural prepping among individual early employees, not an official corporate operational strategy or facility purchase by Anthropic"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 833,
        "endIndex": 995,
        "text": "Anthropic CEO Dario Amodei has publicly distanced himself and current leadership from EA as a formal movement, even as safety research remains central to the firm"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
